    "done_when": "Done when a log under the run directory, opening with its revision and literal command, records the number of live pointers present when the job runs, and for each of at least 6 consecutive ticks over them: the tick's seconds, the process RSS after it, the tracemalloc peak during it, and the 15 allocation sites holding the most retained memory after it, each with its size and object count. The log ends with the sites whose retained size grew in every tick. The station store the job writes is a temporary root, and the job records the newest mtime under ~/.config/reckon/crew/live and the station store before and after, showing it wrote neither. The fragment names, for each site holding more than 100 MB or growing every tick, the function and the cache or structure that holds the memory, with one figure of retained memory by site across the ticks. The review-index views in reckon/crew/review_records.py ( _DOCUMENT_STAT_VIEWS , _STORE_INDEXES , _DOCUMENT_MAPS , each a decoded copy of the roughly 4.8 MB review index) are attributed to that module by name, and any of them growing per tick is reported as a keying defect. The log also records du -sh /dev/shm/* on the fleet node at the job's start, because shared memory counts against the fleet job's cgroup. Positive control: the same harness run with a test-only module-level list that grows by 50 MB per tick attributes at least 45 MB of retained growth per tick to that list's allocation site; a census that cannot see it does not meet this section.",
    "estimated_hours": 1.5,
    "goal": "take a tracemalloc census of the station across six ticks",
